# 3. PERMIT REQUEST AND APPROVAL WORKFLOW

Implement a strict role-based Permit-to-Work approval system.

Approval hierarchy:

STEP 1 – PERMIT REQUESTER

Any authorized logged-in employee or contractor can submit a permit request.

Requester can:
- Create Permit Request.
- View Own Permit Requests.
- View Permit Status.
- Edit permitted request details before submission.
- Request Permit Extension.
- Request Permit Closure.
- Request Permit Revalidation.
- View Approval Comments.
- Upload Supporting Documents.

After submitting a permit:
- Lock the original submitted request fields.
- Do not allow the requester to edit or overwrite submitted details.
- Requester must not have Approve or Reject permissions.
- Requester must not have Delete permission.
- Requester can only request an extension or closure through the defined workflow.
- All changes must be recorded in the audit trail.

STEP 2 – DEPARTMENT HEAD / DEPARTMENT MANAGER

The relevant department head receives the submitted permit request.

Department Head permissions:
- View assigned department permit requests.
- Review the work scope.
- Verify manpower and work requirements.
- Review JSA/HIRA.
- Review required precautions.
- Add review comments.
- Approve the departmental stage.
- Reject the request with mandatory reasons.
- Return the request for clarification where permitted.

Department Head must NOT have:
- Final Safety Approval.
- Permission to bypass Safety approval.
- Global permit deletion.
- Super Admin permissions.

STEP 3 – SAFETY DEPARTMENT

After Department Head approval, the request must automatically move to the Safety Department.

Safety Department permissions:
- Review complete permit request.
- Verify risk assessments.
- Verify control measures.
- Verify isolation requirements.
- Verify gas testing where applicable.
- Verify PPE.
- Verify emergency arrangements.
- Verify legal and site-specific requirements.
- Approve final permit.
- Reject permit with mandatory remarks.
- Return permit for correction.
- Suspend permit.
- Revalidate permit where authorized.
- Close permit where authorized.
- Cancel permit where authorized.

ONLY authorized Safety Approvers can provide FINAL PERMIT APPROVAL.

A permit must never become Active or Issued before final Safety approval.

Approval workflow:

Requester Submission
        ↓
Department Head Review
        ↓
Department Head Approval
        ↓
Safety Department Review
        ↓
Safety Final Approval
        ↓
Permit Issued
        ↓
Work Execution
        ↓
Permit Closure

If Department Head rejects:
Return to requester with rejection reason.

If Safety rejects:
Return to requester with rejection reason and approval history.

Every stage must record:
- User ID
- Name
- Role
- Department
- Action performed
- Date and time
- Comments
- Previous status
- New status

# 4. PERMIT SECURITY AND CONTROL RULES

Implement the following strict rules:

1. Requester cannot approve their own permit.
2. Requester cannot reject their own permit.
3. Department Head can approve only the departmental review stage.
4. Department Head cannot issue final permit approval.
5. Only authorized Safety Approvers can provide final approval.
6. No user can bypass the approval sequence.
7. No user can modify an already approved permit without a controlled revision.
8. Any change to an approved permit must trigger re-review when it affects scope, risk or controls.
9. Permit deletion must be restricted to Super Admin or specifically authorized Safety administrators, with mandatory reason and audit logging.
10. Prefer soft deletion and archival rather than permanent deletion.
11. Never delete an issued permit's historical records.
12. Prevent self-approval and approval conflicts.
13. Expired permits must automatically become Expired.
14. Suspended permits cannot be used for work until formally revalidated.
15. Extension requests must follow the configured approval workflow.
16. All approval timestamps must be stored accurately.
17. Notifications must be sent at every approval stage.
18. Escalate overdue pending approvals.

